*.log
build/out*/
test/orphans.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# s0.199. slp-plugins is PUBLIC.
#
# build/out*/ matches DIRECTORIES NAMED out*, and matched nothing else.
# build/placeid/ held dealers-unique.csv, queries.csv and header-map.csv
# untracked and unignored - one blanket `git add -A`, which is GitHub
# Desktop's default staging, from publishing 303 dealer addresses and the
# exact query strings built from them.
#
# git check-ignore -v returned NOTHING for build/placeid/ on 2026-09-13.
# That silence was the measurement. These rules are the answer to it.
#
# A tracked file is unaffected by .gitignore, so none of the patterns
# below can drop anything already committed. Verified against the tracked
# set: build/ holds only build-v0NN.py and resolve-placeids.py, and the
# only tracked csv in the repo is test/release-pins.csv. Neither is
# matched here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anything the resolver reads or writes.
build/placeid/
build/**/*.csv
build/**/*.json

# s0.207.  fold15.json is the probe's 15.0.0 REFERENCE DATA, not something the
# resolver reads or writes, and build/probe-fold-drift.py prints FAIL and exits
# when it is not beside the script.  Committing the probe without it ships a
# diagnostic that cannot run from a clone.
#
# It is Unicode mappings only - no dealer records, no keys, no query strings -
# so the s0.199 disclosure rationale above does not reach it.  Withdrawn
# caution, rev35 addendum.
#
# A negation works here because line 27 is a FILE pattern.  It would NOT work
# under build/placeid/, which is a DIRECTORY exclusion - git never descends
# into an excluded directory, so no rule inside it can be reversed.  Both
# directions measured in a throwaway repo, by exit code, 2026-09-14.
!build/fold15.json

# The three brand feeds, and everything derived from them, at any depth.
dlrloc.csv
DLAvalon.csv
DLTahoe.csv
dealers-unique.csv
queries.csv
header-map.csv
anomalies.csv
adjudication.csv
placeids.json
review-DELETE-AFTER-TRIAGE.csv

# s0.207.  build/__pycache__/resolve-placeids.cpython-314.pyc was untracked
# AND unignored on 2026-09-14 - measured, not assumed, by replaying the
# working tree's 48 untracked paths against this file: a blanket `git add -A`
# would have staged it alongside the four intended files.  Compiled bytecode
# in a public repo is noise at best.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Patch scripts are private-repo tooling. build-v0NN.py and
# resolve-placeids.py are tracked here and are not matched by this.
build/patch-*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credential-bearing artefacts. s0.180 found 34 committed WP Rocket
# settings exports across four PRIVATE repos, at least one carrying a
# populated minify_css_key, plus 23 page captures - every store and
# find-a-dealer capture carries the SLP REST key in the inline slplus
# JSON, because SLP emits it into every page.
#
# The private repo gained these rules at rev33. This one had none, and a
# public repo is the worse place for a key by a wide margin.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
wp-rocket-settings-*.json
view-source_*.html
bk-*
*.sql
.env
